    "result_text": "Owner responses now include `ownerSegment`, and the full test suite passes: 29 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, including the two new acceptance tests.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: added a read-only string property `ownerSegment` to the Owner schema, next to `timezone`, with the spec text as its description. The `OwnerDto` class is generated from this file, so the new field comes through automatically.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: added a mapping for `ownerSegment` and a method `toOwnerSegment(owner)` that builds the value:\n  - **Tier:** `PREMIUM` when the membership level is 3 or more (new constant `PREMIUM_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL = 3`), otherwise `STANDARD`.\n  - **Area:** `METRO` when the owner's locality is one of the known regions already listed in `CITY_REGIONS` (NSW, VIC, QLD), otherwise `REGIONAL`. So an `UNKNOWN` locality gives `REGIONAL`.\n\nThe segment is calculated when the owner is returned, the same way `timezone` and `ageBand` are, so nothing new is stored in the database.\n\nThe two acceptance tests only cover the `STANDARD_METRO` and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` cases. No test covers the `PREMIUM` tier, which needs membership level 3 or more.",
